From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:08:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov5693: Do not offer the binned mode on
 non-continuous clock links

On IPU6 machines whose front camera is mounted upside down (Microsoft
Surface Pro 7+, Pro 8, Pro 9) every request for 1280x720 or less returns
no frames: libcamera picks the 1296x972 binned mode for it, each buffer
comes back with the error flag set and the receiver logs "csi2-2 error:
Frame sync error" for every frame. A video call at 720p gets nothing,
while 1920x1080, which uses the full 2592x1944 readout, works.

The binned readout itself is not what fails. On a Surface Pro 9 (IPU6,
two lanes, non-continuous clock) raw capture of the binned mode gives

  both flips off     20 of 20 buffers good, 57.3 fps
  HFLIP only         all buffers in error (284 in 10 s)
  VFLIP only         all buffers in error (284 in 10 s)
  both flips on      all buffers in error (283 in 10 s)

and the full readout with both flips on gives 20 of 20 good buffers at
28.6 fps. In the failing cases frame starts still arrive at 57 Hz and one
error buffer is returned for every two of them. The ipu-bridge reports a
rotation of 180 degrees for these machines, so libcamera turns both flips
on. Why the flipped binned readout upsets the receiver is not known.

The driver cannot make the binned size depend on the flips: user space
enumerates the frame sizes once with the flips cleared, and sets the
flips only when it applies the format it chose from that list. So leave
binning out of enum_frame_size and set_fmt altogether when the endpoint
has a non-continuous clock, which is what the ipu-bridge requests for
the IPU6. libcamera then finds 2592x1944 as the only sensor size and
uses it for every stream size.

What is given up on such links: the binned mode also for users who keep
the flips off, where it works; its 57 fps, as the full readout tops out
at 28.6 fps; and the lower readout, link and debayering load of a frame
with a quarter of the pixels. With libcamera's software ISP a 1280x720
stream becomes a centre crop of the full frame instead of a view of the
whole binned frame, as that ISP crops and does not scale. Links with a
continuous clock keep both sizes.

Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/issues/2234
Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/pull/2252
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
index 37f24f4d6..47a72895b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
@@ -771,6 +771,21 @@ static int ov5693_detect(struct ov5693_device *ov5693)
 
 /* V4L2 Framework callbacks */
 
+/*
+ * On a CSI-2 link with a non-continuous clock the 2x2 binned readout only
+ * delivers frames while both flips are off. With either flip on the receiver
+ * reports a frame sync error for every frame and all buffers come back with
+ * the error flag set, where the full readout streams with any flip setting.
+ *
+ * The flips are controls set after the frame sizes were enumerated, and a
+ * sensor mounted upside down has both of them turned on by user space, so
+ * binning cannot follow them. Do not offer it on such a link at all.
+ */
+static unsigned int ov5693_max_binning(const struct ov5693_device *ov5693)
+{
+	return ov5693->clock_ncont ? 1 : 2;
+}
+
 static unsigned int __ov5693_calc_vts(u32 height)
 {
 	/*
@@ -852,12 +867,13 @@ static int ov5693_set_fmt(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 
 	/*
 	 * We can only support setting either the dimensions of the crop rect
-	 * or those dimensions binned (separately) by a factor of two.
+	 * or, where binning is usable, those dimensions binned (separately)
+	 * by a factor of two.
 	 */
-	hratio = clamp_t(unsigned int,
-			 DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(crop->width, width), 1, 2);
-	vratio = clamp_t(unsigned int,
-			 DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(crop->height, height), 1, 2);
+	hratio = clamp_t(unsigned int, DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(crop->width, width),
+			 1, ov5693_max_binning(ov5693));
+	vratio = clamp_t(unsigned int, DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(crop->height, height),
+			 1, ov5693_max_binning(ov5693));
 
 	fmt = __ov5693_get_pad_format(ov5693, state, format->pad,
 				      format->which);
@@ -1063,7 +1079,8 @@ static int ov5693_enum_frame_size(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	struct ov5693_device *ov5693 = to_ov5693_sensor(sd);
 	struct v4l2_rect *__crop;
 
-	if (fse->index > 1 || fse->code != MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SBGGR10_1X10)
+	if (fse->index >= ov5693_max_binning(ov5693) ||
+	    fse->code != MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SBGGR10_1X10)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	__crop = __ov5693_get_pad_crop(ov5693, state, fse->pad, fse->which);
